================================================================
  VDF128_T4 v2 — Eval/Verify CPU benchmark
  MCL-VDF128-BENCH-2026-0905-002   engine: mcl_core v8.1.3 + sidecar
  HW: Apple M1 Pro, 8 logical cores
================================================================

--- PART 1: Eval throughput (sequential, single core) ---
  burn-in B=10000: 0.414 ms (fixed Eval overhead)
  N              best (s)     iters/s        ns/iter     
  1000000        0.0290       3.443e+07      29.046      
  10000000       0.2921       3.423e+07      29.212      
  100000000      2.9345       3.408e+07      29.345      

--- PART 2: Verify via checkpoints (k parallel segments) ---
  Eval(N=1e8, incl. burn-in): 2.9911 s  -> y = 3ee5da21...
  k     verify (s)   Eval/Verify    bit-exact 
  1     2.9306       1.02           yes       
  2     1.4855       2.01           yes       
  4     0.7627       3.92           yes       
  8     0.4620       6.47           yes       
  16    0.4463       6.70           yes       

--- PART 3: end-to-end Eval (incl. burn-in + hashing) ---
  N              wall (s)     note            
  10000          0.0006       burn-in dominates
  1000000        0.0295                       
  10000000       0.2925                       
  100000000      2.9225                       

Notes: single-core Eval by construction (Gauss-Seidel dependency);
Verify parallelism is over checkpoint segments, so the Eval/Verify
wall-clock ratio grows with k up to the core count. FPGA Eval/Verify
measurement on Tang 138K Pro is a separate, pending record.
